  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Roberto González Barrera was a Mexican businessman who founded the corn-flour group Gruma with his father in Cerralvo. After leaving school as a child, he helped build an international food business. He later led the investor group that bought Banorte, whose banking shares became the largest part of his personal fortune.",
    "html": "<p>Roberto González Barrera was a Mexican businessman who founded the corn-flour group Gruma with his father in Cerralvo. After leaving school as a child, he helped build an international food business. He later led the investor group that bought Banorte, whose banking shares became the largest part of his personal fortune.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 51,
    "confidence": {
