  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Food industrialist Roberto González Barrera helped make tortilla dough easier to store and prepare. Gruma’s dried maize flour addressed the short life of fresh dough and required only the addition of water. Working with his father, he developed a product that reduced preparation time and could be kept for later use.\n\nHe also used the company’s production capabilities in disaster relief. Through Grupo Industrial Maseca, González Barrera supplied flour to communities affected by hurricanes, floods and droughts. Mobile tortilla-making units could operate independently in stricken areas, turning the donated flour into hot food for families.",
    "html": "<p>Food industrialist Roberto González Barrera helped make tortilla dough easier to store and prepare. Gruma’s dried maize flour addressed the short life of fresh dough and required only the addition of water. Working with his father, he developed a product that reduced preparation time and could be kept for later use.</p>\r\n<p>He also used the company’s production capabilities in disaster relief. Through Grupo Industrial Maseca, González Barrera supplied flour to communities affected by hurricanes, floods and droughts. Mobile tortilla-making units could operate independently in stricken areas, turning the donated flour into hot food for families.</p>\r\n",
